title: Dashboard › Requests table › Sort the rows
route: /dashboard
intro: Every heading of the table sorts the rows. Each is a button, so the keyboard works too. A heading goes ascending, then descending, then back to the page's own order (the ones that need you today first, then the longest in their state). The sort is not saved in the address.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Dashboard is open\nHeadings of the authorizations table"
screen h1 "Nine headings can sort\nCase, Payer, Service, Status, Days in state, Units, Window, Next action, Owner\nEach shows a small up and down arrow"
click c1 "Click a heading\nOr Tab to it and press Enter or Space"
decision d1 "Is this heading already the sorted one?"
process p1 "No: the sort starts on this heading, ascending\nThe arrow points up; the heading is marked ascending for a screen reader"
decision d2 "Which way is it sorted now?"
process p2 "Ascending, so the next click sorts descending\nThe arrow points down"
process p3 "Descending, so the next click clears the sort\nBack to the page's own order"
process p4 "Rows that tie keep the page's own order\nRows with nothing to sort by stay last either way"
process p5 "Table goes back to its first 8 rows\nThe sentence under the title says 'Sorted by days in state, lowest first.'"
screen sc "Rows in the new order\n'Showing 8 of 40'"

group gKeys "What each heading sorts by"
  screen k1 "Case\nThe ID, A to Z with numbers in order: D-3272 before D-3279, R-0870 before R-1021"
  screen k2 "Payer and Service\nThe short payer name, or the level of care, A to Z"
  screen k3 "Status\nThe word shown, A to Z"
  screen k4 "Days in state\nThe time in the state, shortest to longest"
  screen k5 "Units and Window\nUnits left, and the end date; cases with no approval stay last"
  screen k6 "Next action and Owner\nThe words shown, A to Z"
endgroup

process p6 "Menus, chips and 'Needs me today' keep the sort\nLeaving the page or reloading clears it"
goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Requests table › Order, rows and paging"
goto g2 "Continues in: Dashboard › Requests table › Days in state and the CMS decision time"

s1 --> h1 --> c1 --> d1
d1 -->|No| p1 --> p4
d1 -->|Yes| d2
d2 -->|Ascending| p2 --> p4
d2 -->|Descending| p3 --> p5
p4 --> p5 --> sc
sc --> p6 --> g1
h1 --> k1 & k2 & k3 & k4 & k5 & k6
k4 -.-> g2
